            <div xml:id="d621">

                <pb facs="0625" n="615" sameAs="frus:frus1937v05/pg615"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.52/2345: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Daniels</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-10-26T16:00:00-05:00">October 26, 1937—4
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>210. Reference telegram October 23, 9 a.m. from Guaymas.<anchor n="30"
                        xml:id="d621-f1"/> Please look into point raised by Yepis that decision to
                    dotate eight instead of four hectares of Yaqui Valley land to each applicant for
                    land is illegal. Presumably Vice Consul has in mind article 47 of Agrarian Code,
                    and the Department understands that land in question is irrigated.</p>
                <p>If you consider point well taken please take up matter with appropriate
                    authorities.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
